<div id="subhead"><h1 id="docs-heading">Project Docs</h1></div>
<div id="bar">&nbsp;</div>
<div id="all" class="docs-page">
    <div id="basicinfo" class="docs-body">
        <h2>Stack in one paragraph</h2>
        <p>
            No framework, just Node's <code>node:http</code> plus a small core. Pages are EJS templates
            that compile once at boot and auto-escape every interpolated value. Data lives in two SQLite
            files accessed through Drizzle ORM. Client scripts are TypeScript built to ES5 for IE11 and a
            module bundle for modern browsers.
        </p>

        <h2>Where things live</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>server.ts</b> - boot, page routes and crawler files</li>
            <li><b>src/core/</b> - application pipeline, router, context, sessions, cache, static files, security, errors and views</li>
            <li><b>src/routes/</b> - API endpoints grouped by site area, all guarded and rate-limited</li>
            <li><b>src/views/</b> - EJS templates; shared chrome in partials/</li>
            <li><b>src/styles/</b> - tokens, site, forms, admin, web and dashboard CSS</li>
            <li><b>src/lib/db/</b> - Drizzle schemas and query clients</li>
            <li><b>src/server/queries/</b> - data access used by routes</li>
            <li><b>src/client/</b> - browser scripts, compiled to ES5 at build</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Domains and resources</h2>
        <p>
            The directory covers six Teaching and Learning domains: Knowing Our Students, Strategies for
            Learning, Evidence of Learning, Crafting the Curriculum, Professional Growth and Contribution to
            Workplace Positivity. Each accepted tool has strand flags for the first four domains and
            write-ups for all six. Additional manual or video links are stored as resources.
        </p>

        <h2>Commands</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>pnpm run dev</code> - server and asset watchers</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run build</code> - server, views, CSS and client bundles into dist/</li>
            <li><code>pnpm start</code> - production serve from dist/</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check</code> - types, lint and audit</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check:full</code> - check, unit tests, views and hot reload</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check:flows</code> - temporary-database end-to-end flows</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check:seo</code> - metadata, sitemap, feed and preview images</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run check:contrast</code> - WCAG contrast matrix</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run parity</code> - snapshot render comparison</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run db:reset</code> - recreate dev databases with demo data</li>
            <li><code>pnpm run setup</code> - create or rotate the operator account</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Themes, payments and safety</h2>
        <p>
            One theme cookie drives both sites. Cookies are signed, versioned and revalidated against the
            database. CSRF uses a signed, expiring token. Stripe is the only enabled payment method; checkout
            is refused when webhook verification is not configured. Demo seeds never overwrite a populated
            database.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

